---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import CTASection from '../../components/CTASection.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Cabinet Painting vs Replacement in Kissimmee: Which Saves More?"
  description="Should you paint or replace kitchen cabinets? Cost comparison, durability, and when each option makes sense for Central Florida homes."
  ogImage="/images/painting.jpg"
  schema={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@graph": [
      {
        "@type": "Article",
        "@id": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/cabinet-painting-vs-replacement-kissimmee/#article",
        "headline": "Cabinet Painting vs Replacement in Kissimmee: Which Saves More?",
        "description": "Cabinet painting vs replacement cost comparison for Kissimmee kitchens. When to paint, when to replace.",
        "author": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "GO PRO HOME IMPROVEMENTS INC."
        },
        "publisher": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "GO PRO HOME IMPROVEMENTS INC.",
          "logo": {
            "@type": "ImageObject",
            "url": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/images/logo.png"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
        "@id": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/cabinet-painting-vs-replacement-kissimmee/#breadcrumbs",
        "itemListElement": [
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 1,
            "name": "Home",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com"
          },
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 2,
            "name": "Guides",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides"
          },
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 3,
            "name": "Cabinet Painting vs Replacement",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/cabinet-painting-vs-replacement-kissimmee"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }}
>
  <Header />

  <section class="bg-gopro-charcoal text-white py-16 border-b-4 border-gopro-orange">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <nav class="text-sm mb-6 font-sans">
        <a href="/" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-gopro-orange transition-colors">Home</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-gray-500">/</span>
        <a href="/guides" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-gopro-orange transition-colors">Guides</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-gray-500">/</span>
        <span class="text-white">Cabinet Painting vs Replacement</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-4 tracking-tight">Cabinet Painting vs Replacement in Kissimmee</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 max-w-3xl font-sans">
        Cost comparison, durability, and when each option makes sense for Central Florida kitchens.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-padding">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
          <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6 font-sans">
            Kitchen cabinet refresh in <a href="/areas/kissimmee" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Kissimmee</a> and <a href="/areas/orlando" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Orlando</a> comes down to two options: <a href="/services/interior-exterior-painting" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">painting</a> existing cabinets or full replacement. Painting costs 1/5 to 1/10 the price of new cabinets, but it only works if the cabinet boxes and doors are structurally sound. Here's how to decide which makes sense for your budget and goals.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Cabinet Painting vs Replacement: Cost Comparison</h2>
          
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Cabinet Painting Cost</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            <strong>Average kitchen (10-15 cabinets, 20-30 doors/drawers):</strong> $2,000-$4,500
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Small kitchen (5-8 cabinets):</strong> $1,200-$2,500</li>
            <li><strong>Large kitchen (18-25 cabinets):</strong> $4,500-$7,500</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Includes cleaning, sanding, priming, two coats of paint or stain, and new hardware (optional). Takes 3-5 days including dry time. Kitchen is usable within 24 hours, fully cured in 7-10 days.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Cabinet Replacement Cost</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            <strong>Average kitchen (10-15 cabinets, stock or semi-custom):</strong> $8,000-$25,000
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Stock cabinets (Home Depot, Lowe's):</strong> $8,000-$15,000</li>
            <li><strong>Semi-custom cabinets:</strong> $15,000-$30,000</li>
            <li><strong>Custom cabinets:</strong> $25,000-$50,000+</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Includes cabinet removal, disposal, new cabinets, installation, countertop reinstall or replacement, plumbing/electrical adjustments, and paint touch-up. Takes 1-3 weeks. Kitchen is unusable during install.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gopro-orange/10 border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6 my-8">
            <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
              <strong>Cost comparison:</strong> Painting cabinets costs 1/5 to 1/10 the price of full replacement. For a $15,000 replacement budget, painting the same kitchen runs $2,500-$4,000. That leaves $11,000-$12,500 for new countertops, backsplash, appliances, or flooring—a much bigger visual impact for the same money.
            </p>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">When Cabinet Painting Makes Sense</h2>
          
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">1. Cabinets Are Structurally Sound</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Doors close properly, hinges work, boxes aren't sagging or water-damaged. Most Central Florida homes built in the 2000s-2010s have solid wood or plywood cabinets that paint beautifully. Particle board cabinets (common in 1980s-1990s builds) can be painted if they're in good shape, but they don't hold up as well long-term.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">2. You Like the Current Layout</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Painting doesn't change cabinet size, door style, or layout. If you need more storage, taller uppers, or a different configuration, painting won't help. Replacement is the only option for layout changes.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">3. Budget Is Limited</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            If you have $3,000-$5,000 for a kitchen refresh, painting cabinets + new hardware + fresh backsplash delivers a huge visual upgrade. Spending the same amount on partial cabinet replacement leaves you with an unfinished kitchen.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">4. Quick Turnaround</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Cabinet painting takes 3-5 days. Replacement takes 1-3 weeks (longer if countertops need custom fabrication). For <a href="/guides/kissimmee-vacation-rental-refresh" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">vacation rental</a> flips or homes about to list, painting is faster.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">5. You Want to Change the Color</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Dark oak cabinets → white or gray = instant modern look. Honey oak → navy or charcoal = contemporary style. Painting lets you match current trends without replacing functional cabinets.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">When Cabinet Replacement Makes Sense</h2>
          
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">1. Cabinets Are Damaged</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Water damage (swollen particle board, delamination), broken hinges, sagging shelves, cracked doors. Painting doesn't fix structural problems. If drawers stick, doors don't close, or shelves are bowing, replacement is the better choice.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">2. You Want to Change the Layout</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            More storage, taller uppers, deeper lowers, open shelving, or a pantry cabinet. Painting keeps the existing footprint. Layout changes require replacement.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">3. Door Style Is Dated</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Flat slab doors and shaker-style doors paint well and look modern. But arched cathedral doors, heavy raised panels, or ornate carvings still look dated even after painting. If door style is the issue, consider replacing just the doors ($1,500-$4,000) and painting the cabinet boxes.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">4. Full Remodel Is Planned</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            If you're replacing countertops, moving plumbing, adding an island, or reconfiguring appliances, replace cabinets at the same time. Painting makes sense for cosmetic updates only, not full remodels.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">What About Refacing?</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Cabinet refacing (replacing doors and drawer fronts, applying veneer to boxes) costs $4,000-$10,000—halfway between painting and full replacement. It updates the look without full demo, but you're still stuck with the existing layout and cabinet boxes. Most clients choose either painting (if boxes are fine) or full replacement (if layout needs to change).
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Durability: How Long Does Painted Cabinets Last?</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Professional cabinet painting (proper prep, primer, quality paint) lasts 7-12 years in Central Florida kitchens. Factors that affect longevity:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Paint quality:</strong> We use Benjamin Moore Advance or Sherwin-Williams ProClassic (cabinet-grade paint), not wall paint. Cabinet paint cures harder and resists chips.</li>
            <li><strong>Prep work:</strong> Cleaning, sanding, and deglossing ensure paint bonds. Skipping prep = peeling within 2 years.</li>
            <li><strong>Humidity:</strong> Florida's humidity slows dry time. We wait 24 hours between coats (most DIYers rush it and get soft, sticky paint).</li>
            <li><strong>Usage:</strong> High-traffic kitchens (large families, vacation rentals) see more wear than low-use kitchens.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Professionally painted cabinets outlast DIY paint jobs by 3-5 years because of prep quality and paint selection.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">The Middle Ground: Paint Boxes, Replace Doors</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            If your cabinet boxes are solid but doors are damaged or dated, consider a hybrid approach:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li>Paint cabinet boxes and frames</li>
            <li>Order new slab or shaker doors ($50-$150 per door)</li>
            <li>Install new soft-close hinges and hardware</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            <strong>Cost:</strong> $3,000-$7,000 for an average kitchen. Gives you modern door style + updated color for 40-60% less than full replacement.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">ROI: Which Adds More Value?</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            For resale, fresh cabinets (painted or new) add value. But the return depends on your starting point and budget:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Painting cabinets:</strong> $2,500 cost → $3,000-$5,000 value increase (ROI: 120-200%)</li>
            <li><strong>Cabinet replacement:</strong> $15,000 cost → $10,000-$15,000 value increase (ROI: 65-100%)</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Painting delivers higher ROI because the cost is low. But if your cabinets are falling apart, replacement is necessary to sell the home at all. Buyers in <a href="/areas/celebration" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Celebration</a>, <a href="/areas/orlando" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Orlando</a>, and Central Florida expect functional kitchens—broken cabinets kill offers.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Cabinet Painting Process</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Here's what professional cabinet painting includes:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Day 1:</strong> Remove doors, drawer fronts, and hardware. Label everything. Clean cabinets (grease remover). Sand and degloss. Mask countertops, backsplash, appliances.</li>
            <li><strong>Day 2:</strong> Prime cabinet boxes and doors. Let dry 4-6 hours. Light sanding. First coat of paint.</li>
            <li><strong>Day 3:</strong> Second coat of paint. Let dry overnight.</li>
            <li><strong>Day 4:</strong> Reinstall doors and drawer fronts. Install new hardware (if ordered). Clean up.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Kitchen is usable within 24 hours (be gentle with doors). Full cure takes 7-10 days—avoid heavy scrubbing or stacking dishes against doors during that time.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Paint cabinets if they're structurally sound, you like the layout, and budget is $2,000-$5,000. Replace cabinets if they're damaged, you need layout changes, or you're doing a full remodel. Painting costs 1/5 to 1/10 the price of replacement and delivers 120-200% ROI. Hybrid option: paint boxes, replace doors for $3,000-$7,000.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-8 my-8">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide">Need Cabinet Painting in Kissimmee?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-6">
              Professional prep, cabinet-grade paint, new hardware. Transform your kitchen without the cost of replacement.
            </p>
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4">
              <a href="/estimate" class="btn-primary">
                Get Free Estimate
              </a>
              <a href="tel:4072446873" class="btn-secondary">
                Call (407) 244-6873
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200">
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 font-sans">
              <a href="/guides" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">← Back to All Guides</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTASection
    title="Professional Cabinet Painting"
    description="Modern color, professional finish, fraction of replacement cost."
  />

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
